From 2de43c9224e8d6eb149baf9eda4951dc9220218b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Aug 2025 07:22:34 -1000
Subject: [PATCH 27/63] add vmnet networking option to qemu manager for macos
 users

Summary:
# Motivation:
slirp does full emultation of the software stack, but can be sub-par in performance.
# Overview:
- add vmnet option to qemu_manager.cpp

# Reference:
- goldfish qemu fork arguments
https://www.internalfb.com/code/aosp-platform-external-qemu/[emu-35-2-release-meta%3A90f69a72efd89a27b95c043317bc073a8f1122c4]/android-qemu2-glue/main.cpp?lines=2866-2879

# Note:
when switching back to slirp
```
sudo rm -rf /tmp/modem_simulator*
```

Test Plan:

Note (`sudo` is required)
```
m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz -k &> ~/build.logs.txt && sudo HOME=/Users/achong/n-16/out/host/darwin-x86 out/host/darwin-x86/bin/launch_cvd  \
--vm_manager=qemu_cli  --system_image_dir=/Users/achong/n-16/out/host/darwin-x86 \
--qemu_binary_dir=/Users/achong/qemu/build \
--enable_host_uwb=false -device_external_network=vmnet \
--vhost_user_vsock --enable_audio=true
```

network ping is lower
```
adb shell ping 1.1.1.1
PING 1.1.1.1 (1.1.1.1) 56(84) bytes of data.
64 bytes from 1.1.1.1: icmp_seq=1 ttl=59 time=15.4 ms
```
